---
# Project style enforcement (see docs/DESIGN.md + memory: cpp-style):
#  - encapsulated data members are m_snake_case, no trailing underscore
#    (Private/Protected only). Public data-bag / ABI-POD fields stay plain:
#    m_ on them is a REVIEW rule, not automation. readability-identifier-naming
#    cannot tell an aggregate POD from a struct-with-methods (both are "public
#    members"), so leaving PublicMember* unset is what lets the D26 wire PODs
#    (Command/MidiMessage/OutEvent) keep positional plain fields and clean
#    designated init (.status =, not .m_status =).
#  - every control-flow body is braced.
#  - aggregate literals use designated initializers (.field =).
#  - cognitive complexity is a warning for now, promoted to a gate once the
#    command dispatch (Shell::exec_now) is split into per-domain cmd_* handlers.
Checks: >
  -*,
  readability-identifier-naming,
  readability-braces-around-statements,
  modernize-use-designated-initializers,
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity
HeaderFilterRegex: 'apps/|components/'
# The two opinionated new checks ramp in as warnings first: designated-init
# fires hard on the core's dense positional data tables (StyleEvent, wire PODs)
# where positional is idiomatic, and cognitive-complexity flags exec_now/on_tick
# pending their split. Migrate + NOLINT incrementally, then promote to gate.
WarningsAsErrors: '*,-readability-function-cognitive-complexity,-modernize-use-designated-initializers'
CheckOptions:
  readability-identifier-naming.PrivateMemberCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.PrivateMemberPrefix: m_
  readability-identifier-naming.ProtectedMemberCase: lower_case
  readability-identifier-naming.ProtectedMemberPrefix: m_
  readability-braces-around-statements.ShortStatementLines: 0
  modernize-use-designated-initializers.IgnoreSingleElementAggregates: 'true'
  modernize-use-designated-initializers.RestrictToPODTypes: 'false'
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity.Threshold: '25'
  readability-function-cognitive-complexity.IgnoreMacros: 'true'
...
